.IX Title "Clownfish::Docs::BuildingProjects 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::Docs::BuildingProjects 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::Docs::BuildingProjects \- Building Clownfish projects in C environments
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The following steps are required to build a project that uses
Clownfish:
.IP \(bu 4
Run the \f(CW\*(C`cfc\*(C'\fR command-line application (Clownfish compiler) to
generate C headers, C source files, and documentation.
.IP \(bu 4
Include the C headers generated by the Clownfish compiler in your
own code to work with Clownfish objects.
.IP \(bu 4
Compile an additional C source file generated by CFC.
.IP \(bu 4
Link your object code, the object code from the generated file,
and the Clownfish runtime library.
.SS "Running cfc"
.IX Subsection "Running cfc"
.Vb 3
\&    cfc [\-\-source=<dir>] [\-\-include=<dir>] [\-\-parcel=<name>]
\&        \-\-dest=<dir>
\&        [\-\-header=<file>] [\-\-footer=<file>]
.Ve
.PP
\fI–source\fR
.IX Subsection "–source"
.PP
Every \f(CW\*(C`\-\-source\*(C'\fR argument adds a directory to the list of source
directories to search for source parcels. For every source parcel
found, CFC generates C headers, a C source file, and documentation.
.PP
The source directories are scanned for Clownfish parcel definitions
(\f(CW\*(C`.cfp\*(C'\fR), Clownfish headers (\f(CW\*(C`.cfh\*(C'\fR), and standalone documentation
in Markdown format (\f(CW\*(C`.md\*(C'\fR).
.PP
This option may be specified multiple times.
.PP
\fI–include\fR
.IX Subsection "–include"
.PP
Every \f(CW\*(C`\-\-include\*(C'\fR argument adds a directory to the list of include
directories. CFC generates C headers for parcels from an include
directory only if they’re required by a source parcel or if they’re
specified with the \f(CW\*(C`\-\-parcel\*(C'\fR option. Only C headers are generated
for included parcels, no C source code or documentation.
.PP
The include directories are scanned for Clownfish parcel
definitions (\f(CW\*(C`.cfp\*(C'\fR) and Clownfish headers (\f(CW\*(C`.cfh\*(C'\fR).
.PP
After the directories specified on the command-line, the following
directories are processed:
.IP \(bu 4
Directories from the environment variable \f(CW\*(C`CLOWNFISH_INCLUDE\*(C'\fR.
This variable contains a colon-separated list of directories.
.IP \(bu 4
On UNIX-like systems \f(CW\*(C`/usr/local/share/clownfish/include\*(C'\fR and
\&\f(CW\*(C`/usr/share/clownfish/include\*(C'\fR.
.PP
This option may be specified multiple times.
.PP
\fI–parcel\fR
.IX Subsection "–parcel"
.PP
Adds a parcel to the list of prerequisite parcels to make sure that
its C headers are generated. This is useful when running without the
\&\f(CW\*(C`\-\-source\*(C'\fR option. For example, a project that doesn’t define its
own Clownfish classes can generate the C headers for the Clownfish
runtime with:
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    cfc \-\-parcel=Clownfish \-\-dest=autogen
.Ve
.PP
This option may be specified multiple times.
.PP
\fI–dest\fR
.IX Subsection "–dest"
.PP
The destination directory for generated files. By convention,
the name \f(CW\*(C`autogen\*(C'\fR is used.
.PP
CFC creates the following subdirectories in the destination
directory:
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`include\*(C'\fR contains generated C headers.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`sources\*(C'\fR contains generated C source files.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`man\*(C'\fR contains generated man pages.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\f(CW\*(C`share/doc/clownfish\*(C'\fR contains generated HTML documentation.
.PP
This option is required.
.PP
\fI–header\fR
.IX Subsection "–header"
.PP
Specifies a file whose contents are added as a comment on top of
each generated file.
.PP
\fI–footer\fR
.IX Subsection "–footer"
.PP
Specifies a file whose contents are added as a comment on the
bottom of each generated file.
.SS "Including the generated C headers"
.IX Subsection "Including the generated C headers"
The C header files generated with \f(CW\*(C`cfc\*(C'\fR can be found in
\&\f(CW\*(C`autogen/include\*(C'\fR. You should add this directory to your compiler’s
search path, for example using \f(CW\*(C`\-Iautogen/include\*(C'\fR under GCC.
.PP
One C header file is generated for every Clownfish header (.cfh) file.
C code that makes use of a class defined in the .cfh file must include
the respective C header. The Clownfish compiler also creates a few
other internal C header files.
.SS "Compiling the generated source files"
.IX Subsection "Compiling the generated source files"
\&\f(CW\*(C`cfc\*(C'\fR creates one source file for every parcel in
\&\f(CW\*(C`autogen/sources/{parcel_nick}_parcel.c\*(C'\fR. These files must be
compiled with \f(CW\*(C`autogen/include\*(C'\fR added to the header search path.
.SS Linking
.IX Subsection "Linking"
When linking, add the object files of the CFC-generated code created
in the previous step. You must also link the shared library of the
Clownfish runtime (\f(CW\*(C`\-lclownfish\*(C'\fR under GCC).
